 "rule": "Throughput-phase rule (Zenodo 4730157, training_part01 ... 09; used if the user picks that phase, and for the cross-phase test set otherwise; `throughput_split`): the tar parts have no central directory, so the ids of training_part01 are recorded when the part is first streamed, before any model sees them; dev = the 100 smallest part01 ids (they include 21000-21004, inspected for the plan); eligible = the other part01 ids; default_rng(SEED).permutation of the sorted eligible ids: first N_TEST -> test, next N_VAL -> val, valmon = the first N_VALMON val ids in sorted order; train = every other event of the nine parts.",
 "subset_rule": "Throughput subsets (`tp_subsets`; plan sections 6.0, 6.2 and 6.6, with the dev ids of the throughput rule): calib = dev + the next N_CALIB_EXTRA training ids in sorted order (truth kinematics and score weights stored); gbdt = the N_GBDT smallest training ids outside calib; merge_train = the N_MERGE_TRAIN smallest training ids outside calib and gbdt. hnl.trackml.config computes the same lists from the stored training events.",
 "scope": "D1 = throughput with D2 = train_1-sized (the user's decisions, plan section 1.4): only training_part01 and training_part02 are streamed (hnl.trackml.throughput scan), so `make-tp` applies the rule to their recorded ids: dev, val, valmon and test depend on part01 alone, and train is \"every other event\" of the two streamed parts.",
